
%9Syntax:%9

KLIST %|[<mask>]

%9Parameters:%9

    An optional mask passed to the server as the STATS argument.

%9Description:%9

    Sends STATS K to the server of the active window, asking for the list
    of permanent K-lines from the ircd 2.11 configuration. erssi shows the
    server's reply like any other. A command of the tk.pl script; /TK KLIST
    does the same.

    The argument must be a single word (up to 64 characters) - anything
    else is ignored and a plain STATS K is sent. The server decides who
    may see the list.

    Permanent K-lines cannot be removed with /UNTKL - that command only
    applies to tklines from /TKLIST.

%9Examples:%9

    /KLIST
    /KLIST *@*.example.org

%9See also:%9 STATS, TK, TKL, TKLIST, UNTKL

